A `prefix.changed` over two requests that hash to the same head. Nothing moved,
so nothing that compared two digests could have written this row -- and a
cache-miss census reading it would count a mutation the file itself denies.

The row carries no digest of its own on purpose: both are on the `request`
rows, where they cannot contradict each other. This document is what that
arrangement is for -- the contradiction is visible from the two rows above,
rather than hidden inside a third copy.
